#### Phase 3: Add Error Handling and Retry Logic

1. **Implement Retry with Exponential Backoff**

   ```java
   @Component
   public class BatchErrorHandler {
       private final DeadLetterQueuePublisher dlqPublisher;
       private final RetryPolicy retryPolicy;

       public CompletableFuture<Void> handleFailure(
           String topic,
           List<Object> failedBatch,
           Throwable error
       ) {
           return retryBatch(topic, failedBatch, 0)
               .exceptionally(ex -> {
                   // After all retries exhausted, try individual events
                   return fallbackToIndividualPublish(topic, failedBatch);
               });
       }

       private CompletableFuture<Void> retryBatch(
           String topic,
           List<Object> batch,
           int attempt
       ) {
           if (attempt >= retryPolicy.getMaxAttempts()) {
               return CompletableFuture.failedFuture(
                   new MaxRetriesExceededException()
               );
           }

           long backoffMs = retryPolicy.calculateBackoff(attempt);

           return CompletableFuture
               .delayedExecutor(backoffMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)
               .execute(() -> publisher.publishBatch(topic, batch))
               .exceptionally(ex -> retryBatch(topic, batch, attempt + 1));
       }

       private Void fallbackToIndividualPublish(String topic, List<Object> batch) {
           List<Object> failed = new ArrayList<>();

           for (Object event : batch) {
               try {
                   publisher.publishSingle(topic, event).get(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
               } catch (Exception e) {
                   failed.add(event);
               }
           }

           // Send truly failed events to DLQ
           if (!failed.isEmpty()) {
               dlqPublisher.sendToDLQ(topic, failed);
               metrics.counter("batch.dlq.events", "topic", topic).increment(failed.size());
           }

           return null;
       }
   }
   ```

2. **Implement Circuit Breaker (Resilience4j)**

   ```java
   @Configuration
   public class BatchingCircuitBreakerConfig {

       @Bean
       public CircuitBreaker batchPublishCircuitBreaker() {
           CircuitBreakerConfig config = CircuitBreakerConfig.custom()
               .failureRateThreshold(50)                    // Open after 50% failures
               .waitDurationInOpenState(Duration.ofSeconds(30))  // Wait 30s before retry
               .slidingWindowSize(100)                      // Evaluate last 100 calls
               .minimumNumberOfCalls(10)                    // Need 10 calls before evaluation
               .build();

           return CircuitBreaker.of("batch-publisher", config);
       }
   }

   @Component
   public class CircuitBreakerAwarePublisher {
       private final CircuitBreaker circuitBreaker;
       private final AsyncEventPublisher publisher;

       public CompletableFuture<SendResult> publishBatch(String topic, List<Object> batch) {
           return circuitBreaker.executeCompletionStage(
               () -> publisher.publishBatch(topic, batch)
           ).toCompletableFuture();
       }
   }
   ```

