#### Phase 4: Implement Graceful Shutdown

1. **Add Shutdown Hook to Flush Pending Batches**

   ```java
   @Component
   public class EventBatcherShutdownHook {
       private final EventBatcher<?> eventBatcher;

       @PostConstruct
       public void registerShutdownHook() {
           Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
               log.info("Shutdown initiated, flushing pending batches...");

               try {
                   // Stop accepting new events
                   eventBatcher.setAcceptingEvents(false);

                   // Flush all buffers
                   eventBatcher.flushAll();

                   // Wait for pending publishes (max 5 seconds)
                   boolean completed = eventBatcher.awaitCompletion(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);

                   if (completed) {
                       log.info("All batches flushed successfully");
                   } else {
                       log.warn("Timeout waiting for batch flush, {} events may be lost",
                           eventBatcher.getPendingEventCount());
                   }
               } catch (Exception e) {
                   log.error("Error during shutdown flush", e);
               }
           }));
       }
   }
   ```

